{"book":10,"chapter":7,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / GETTING TO KNOW RUST / CHAPTER 7","slides":[{"title":"Three compound types","sub":"Chapter 7 · Tuple, array, vector","short":"Intro","main":"Tuple — different types, array — fixed size, vector — grows.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Compound types","Tuple and array","Vector"],"captions":["A compound type holds several values together","Tuple — different types, fixed size; array — one type, fixed size","Vector — one type, growing size: a relative of the Python list"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"(…)","tone":"blue","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"[…; N]","tone":"blue","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Vec<T>","tone":"blue","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"(i32, f64, &str)","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"[i32; 3]","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"v0","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v1","x":146.0,"y":66.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"2","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v2","x":202.0,"y":66.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"3","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":50.0,"h":32.0,"text":"+ push","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.6,27.7]}]},{"title":"Tuples","sub":"(A, B, C)","short":"Tuples","main":"Access t.0, t.1; destructuring let (x, y, z).","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Creating","Access by number","Destructuring"],"captions":["let t = (3, 4.5, \"text\"); — type (i32, f64, &str): elements of any types","t.0, t.1, t.2 — the number is known at build time, so no square brackets","let (x, y, z) = t; — unpack into variables; () is the empty tuple, a.k.a. unit"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":70.0,"h":36.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":70.0,"h":36.0,"text":"4.5","tone":"green","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"\"text\"","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let t = (3, 4.5, \"text\");","t.0   // 3","t.1   // 4.5"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let (x, y, z) = t;","// x=3, y=4.5, z=\"text\""],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[15.8,26.5]}]},{"title":"Arrays","sub":"[T; N]","short":"Arrays","main":"Length is part of the type; on the stack; [0; 5].","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["[T; N]","Length is part of the type","On the stack"],"captions":["let a = [1, 2, 3]; — type [i32; 3]; [0; 5] — five zeros","[i32; 3] and [i32; 4] are different types; a.len() is the length, a[0] an element","The array lies right on the stack — no heap allocation, so it is very fast"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":90.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":146.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":202.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"[0; 5] → 0 0 0 0 0","size":10.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"[i32; 3]","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"[i32; 4]","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"different types","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":100.0,"y":66.0,"w":110.0,"h":80.0,"text":"stack\n[1, 2, 3]","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":110.0,"h":80.0,"text":"heap\n— not needed","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.5}]],"cues":[12.9,24.2]}]},{"title":"Bounds","sub":"Panic and get","short":"Bounds","main":"The index is checked; get returns an Option.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Out of bounds","Panic","get"],"captions":["a[5] with length 3 is out of bounds; in C it reads foreign memory, in Python it is an IndexError","Rust checks the index on every access and panics; a constant index is caught at build time","a.get(5) returns None instead of panicking — the safe way"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":90.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":146.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":202.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":290.0,"y":56.0,"w":50.0,"h":32.0,"text":"[5]?","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let a = [1, 2, 3];","let i = 5;","a[i]   // panic: index out of bounds"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["a.get(1)   // Some(2)","a.get(5)   // None"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[9.5,23.6]}]},{"title":"Slices","sub":"&[T]","short":"Slices","main":"A reference to a part; slice parameters accept everything.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["&a[1..3]","Type &[T]","Slice parameters"],"captions":["A slice is a reference to part of a sequence: &a[1..3] — elements 1 and 2","Type &[i32] has no length; pointer and length are stored together; nothing is copied","Functions should accept a slice: fn sum(v: &[i32]) takes an array, a vector and part of a vector"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":32.0,"text":"10","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":116.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":32.0,"text":"20","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":182.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":32.0,"text":"30","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":248.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":32.0,"text":"40","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":182.0,"y":60.0,"w":124.0,"h":36.0,"text":"","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.35}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":100.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ptr →","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":100.0,"y":84.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"len = 2","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":260.0,"y":66.0,"text":"&[i32]","size":13.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["fn sum(v: &[i32]) -> i32 { … }","sum(&arr);","sum(&vec);","sum(&vec[1..]);"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.2,32.9]}]},{"title":"Vec","sub":"A growable array","short":"Vec","main":"vec!, push, pop, len; data on the heap.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Creating","push and pop","Heap"],"captions":["vec![1, 2, 3] or Vec::new(): type Vec<i32>","push adds to the end, pop removes the last and returns it, len is the count","The data lies on the heap: a vector can grow while the program runs"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let v = vec![1, 2, 3];","let mut w: Vec<i32> = Vec::new();"],"lang":"rust","size":11.5,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":126.0,"y":60.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":182.0,"y":60.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":282.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":32.0,"text":"4","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":282.0,"y":100.0,"text":"push(4)","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":110.0,"h":60.0,"text":"stack\nptr, len, cap","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":60.0,"text":"heap\n[1, 2, 3, …]","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.4,24.8]}]},{"title":"Access and Option","sub":"get, first, last","short":"Access","main":"v[i] panics, get is safe; Option — \"a value or nothing\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["v[i]","get, first, last","Option"],"captions":["v[0] — like an array; going out of bounds panics","v.get(5) → None, v.first() → Some(&1), v.last() → Some(&3): a vector may be empty","Option<T> — \"a value or nothing\": Some(x) and None; for now unwrap() is enough"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let v = vec![1, 2, 3];","v[0]   // 1","v[9]   // panic!"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["v.get(1)   // Some(&2)","v.get(9)   // None","v.first()  // Some(&1)","v.last()   // Some(&3)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Some(5)\nthere is","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"None\nthere is not","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"x.unwrap() takes the value out","size":10.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[15.8,29.1]}]},{"title":"Iteration","sub":"&v, &mut v, iter","short":"Iteration","main":"for over a reference, over a mutable reference; iterators sum, max, filter.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["for x in &v","&mut v","iter()"],"captions":["for x in &v — look at the elements, take nothing","for x in &mut v { *x += 1; } — change in place; the asterisk reaches the value itself","v.iter().sum(), max(), min(), enumerate(), map, filter — iterator chains"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for x in &v {","    println!(\"{x}\");","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for x in &mut v {","    *x += 1;","}"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let s: i32 = v.iter().sum();","let m = v.iter().max();   // Option","let big: Vec<i32> = v.iter()","    .filter(|x| **x > 1).cloned().collect();"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[16.8,24.5]}]},{"title":"Modifying a vector","sub":"insert, remove, extend","short":"Modifying","main":"Modifying methods; let mut is required.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["insert and remove","extend and clear","mut is required"],"captions":["insert(i, x) inserts at a position; remove(i) deletes by index and returns the value","extend appends another vector, clear empties, contains searches, reverse flips, dedup removes neighboring duplicates","You can change a vector only if it is declared let mut — just like an ordinary variable"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];","v.insert(1, 9);   // [1, 9, 2, 3]","v.remove(0);      // [9, 2, 3]"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["v.extend([7, 8]);","v.contains(&7);   // true","v.reverse();","v.clear();"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let v = vec![1, 2];","v.push(3);   // ✕ cannot borrow as mutable"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[14.6,26.2]}]},{"title":"Sorting and searching","sub":"sort, binary_search","short":"Sorting","main":"sort, sort_by_key, binary_